--------------------------------------------------
PORT PLAN (NO COLLISION)
--------------------------------------------------
- Backend API: 8000
- Postgres: 5433
- Mobile Metro (Expo Go): 8081
- Frontdesk Metro (Sunmi dev build): 8082

--------------------------------------------------
0) ONE-TIME PREREQUISITES
--------------------------------------------------
- Docker Desktop running
- Node + npm installed
- adb installed (Android platform-tools)
- Sunmi USB debugging ON
- Phone and PC on same Wi-Fi for Expo Go (mobile app)

Repo root:
  C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip

--------------------------------------------------
1) START BACKEND (DOCKER)
--------------------------------------------------
From repo root:
  docker compose up -d postgres backend

Health check:
  Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:8000/health
Expected:
  {"status":"ok"}

--------------------------------------------------
2) VERIFY/SET BACKEND CONFIG (IMPORTANT)
--------------------------------------------------
Backend env file:
  backend\.env

Must include:
  otp_test_code=123456
  store_latitude=31.9539
  store_longitude=35.9106

If you changed backend\.env, restart backend:
  docker compose restart backend

--------------------------------------------------
3) RUN MOBILE APP (EXPO GO OVER WIFI)
--------------------------------------------------
Mobile env file is persistent now:
  mobile\.env

Should contain your current PC Wi-Fi IP:
  EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.228:8000

If your PC IP changed, update that value first.
Find IP:
  ipconfig

Start mobile Metro:
  cd mobile
  npx expo start --host lan --port 8081 --clear

On phone:
- Open Expo Go
- Scan QR
- If app was already open, fully close and reopen Expo Go first

--------------------------------------------------
4) RUN FRONTDESK ON SUNMI (USB)
--------------------------------------------------
Plug Sunmi USB and verify:
  adb devices

Set USB reverse tunnels:
  adb reverse --remove-all
  adb reverse tcp:8081 tcp:8082
  adb reverse tcp:8082 tcp:8082
  adb reverse tcp:8000 tcp:8000
  adb reverse --list

Start frontdesk Metro:
  cd frontdesk
  $env:EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"
  npx expo start --host lan --port 8082 --clear

Notes:
- The 8081->8082 reverse is required for Sunmi dev client script loading.
- Frontdesk API uses 127.0.0.1:8000 through USB reverse.

--------------------------------------------------
5) FRONTDESK BUILD / REBUILD (WHEN NEEDED)
--------------------------------------------------
If native or dev build changed:
  cd frontdesk\android
  $env:EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"
  .\gradlew.bat installDebug

If frontdesk is stuck in bad auth/session state:
  adb shell pm clear com.takeasip.frontdesk

--------------------------------------------------
