--------------------------------------------------
Delivery confirm fails if distance bands are missing.
Current active ranges should cover 0-100 km.

If needed, re-create via Admin app/API.
Expected active coverage:
- 0.000 -> 3.000
- 3.000 -> 7.000
- 7.000 -> 12.000
- 12.000 -> 100.000

--------------------------------------------------
7) QUICK SANITY CHECK FLOW
--------------------------------------------------
1. Mobile app: login as CLIENT (0790000101 / 123456)
2. Mobile app: place pickup or delivery order
3. Frontdesk app: order appears in list
4. Frontdesk app: accept order
5. Driver app/account: sees assigned delivery when applicable

--------------------------------------------------
8) TROUBLESHOOTING (FAST)
--------------------------------------------------
A) Mobile OTP shows "Network error"
- Confirm backend health:
    Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:8000/health
- Confirm mobile\.env IP is correct
- Restart mobile Metro with clear cache:
    cd mobile
    npx expo start --host lan --port 8081 --clear
- Fully close Expo Go and rescan QR

B) Frontdesk shows "Unable to load script"
- Ensure these reverses exist:
    adb reverse tcp:8081 tcp:8082
    adb reverse tcp:8082 tcp:8082
- Restart frontdesk Metro on 8082

C) Frontdesk shows "Disconnected"
- Reset app/session and tunnels:
    adb shell pm clear com.takeasip.frontdesk
    adb reverse --remove-all
    adb reverse tcp:8081 tcp:8082
    adb reverse tcp:8082 tcp:8082
    adb reverse tcp:8000 tcp:8000
- Login with FRONTDESK or ADMIN only

D) Confirm order shows server error
- If pickup fails: restart backend and retry
- If delivery fails: verify delivery distance bands + store coordinates exist

E) Wrong account role on frontdesk
- Allowed roles: FRONTDESK, ADMIN
- CLIENT/DRIVER will be rejected by design

--------------------------------------------------
9) STOP EVERYTHING
--------------------------------------------------
- Stop Metro terminals (Ctrl+C)
- Stop backend containers:
    docker compose down
